{"metric":"gowdy","source":[{"metric":"gowdy","system":"areal","fields":["coords","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","metric_components","parameters"],"version":"4b7704b04ffc404f"},{"metric":"gowdy","system":"logarithmic","fields":["coords","inverse_metric_components","metric_components","parameters"],"version":"00c0ee7f96c99056"},{"metric":"gowdy","system":"sphere","fields":["coords","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","metric_components","parameters"],"version":"f4a8fdbd68b170c3"}],"views":[{"id":"areal","label":"Areal time","box":[-0.45,3.2759,-0.3,3.4416],"system":"areal","input":"A polarised wave once round the torus, $Q = 0$, $P = -\\tfrac{\\pi}{4}Y_0(t)\\cos\\theta$, and $\\lambda = \\tfrac{\\pi^2}{16}\\left(\\tfrac{1}{2}t^2\\left(Y_0^2 + Y_1^2\\right) - tY_0Y_1\\cos^2\\theta\\right)$, with $Y_0$ and $Y_1$ the Bessel functions of the second kind at $t$, checked to solve this spacetime's own field equations; as $t \\to 0$, $P \\to \\tfrac{1}{2}\\cos\\theta\\,\\tau$ with $\\tau = -\\ln t$.","caption":["The plane of $t$ and $\\theta$ of the torus universe, each point in the diagram a 2-torus of area $4\\pi^2L^2t$. The metric on it is $L^2t^{-1/2}e^{\\lambda/2}(-dt^2 + d\\theta^2)$, and a conformal factor changes no null direction, so for every wave $p, q = \\arctan(t \\mp \\theta)$ bring it into Minkowski's triangle, where the lines $\\theta = 0$ and $\\theta = 2\\pi$ are one line of the torus.","The singularity $t = 0$ is spacelike, the segment along the bottom, and since $\\theta$ is bounded every line of constant $\\theta$ and every light ray ends at the one point $i^+$, $t \\to \\infty$. A light ray from the singularity crosses the drawing from one edge to the other in the time $2\\pi$."],"layers":[{"kind":"fill","class":"region","points":[[0.0,0.0],[2.8259,0.0],[2.8259,0.0],[2.8259,0.0],[2.8259,0.0],[2.8259,0.0],[2.8259,0.0],[2.8259,0.0],[2.8259,0.0],[2.8259,0.0],[2.8259,0.0],[2.8259,0.0],[2.8259,0.0],[2.8259,0.0],[2.8259,0.0],[2.8259,0.0],[2.8